request.user_message:
Abstract the following semantic predicate cluster into exactly one reusable predicate.

Cluster ID:
unary-014

Cluster Arity:
1

Cluster Members:
[
  {
    "name": "PLANS_POST_ACTION_VERIFICATION",
    "definition": "The reasoning explicitly plans one or more checks to be performed after an action in order to determine whether the action produced the required outcome or final state.",
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "reasoning",
        "type": "reasoning",
        "description": "The reasoning text specifying the future verification checks and their purpose."
      }
    ],
    "assertion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning refers to future verification or checking steps.",
      "The checks are directed at confirming the outcome or final state of a completed or planned action, rather than at initial exploration.",
      "At least one check criterion or target state is identifiable."
    ],
    "exclusion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning only describes exploratory inspection before any relevant action.",
      "The reasoning only reports checks already completed without planning future verification.",
      "The reasoning states a general next step without a validation purpose."
    ]
  },
  {
    "name": "BROADENS_VERIFICATION_BEYOND_REQUIRED_CASES",
    "definition": "The reasoning identifies input conditions or variations that the stated requirements and given test harness do not exercise, and commits to verifying them in order to reduce the risk of undetected failure.",
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "reasoning",
        "type": "reasoning",
        "description": "The agent text naming extra input variations and stating the intention to test them for additional assurance."
      }
    ],
    "assertion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning names at least one concrete input variation not exercised by the stated test harness, such as a size edge case, an alternative memory layout, an alternative data type, a malformed input, or an alternative invocation interface.",
      "The reasoning states that these additional checks will be performed to gain assurance beyond the required tests."
    ],
    "exclusion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning only repeats the tests required by the task specification.",
      "Additional checks are mentioned without identifying any concrete input variation to be exercised.",
      "The extra activity substitutes for required verification rather than extending it, with no additional assurance motive stated."
    ]
  },
  {
    "name": "ANTICIPATES_UNSPECIFIED_EVALUATION_CRITERIA",
    "definition": "The reasoning identifies one or more plausible checks, usage patterns, or evaluation scenarios that an external evaluator, hidden test harness, or checker might apply even though the task specification does not state them, and assesses whether the current solution already satisfies or would survive them.",
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "reasoning",
        "type": "reasoning",
        "description": "Agent text that names unstated evaluation scenarios an external checker might exercise and assesses the solution's robustness against them."
      }
    ],
    "assertion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning names at least one specific check, usage pattern, or scenario that is not stated in the provided task requirements.",
      "The reasoning treats that scenario as a condition an external evaluator or checker might impose on the solution, and assesses whether the solution already handles it or would survive it."
    ],
    "exclusion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning only restates or addresses checks that are explicitly required by the task specification.",
      "The reasoning merely reports results of checks already executed without hypothesizing an unstated external check.",
      "The reasoning describes hypothetical environment or user behaviors without connecting them to evaluation or acceptance of the solution.",
      "The reasoning enumerates a concrete additional input variation and commits to verifying it, rather than assessing robustness against an unstated evaluator check."
    ]
  }
]

Previously Generated Predicate Names:
["CONFIGURES_EVENT_DRIVEN_AUTOMATION", "PREVENTS_SELF_CAUSED_ADVERSE_EFFECTS_THROUGH_CORRECTIVE_ACTION", "EVALUATES_CANDIDATE_AGAINST_ENUMERATED_CONSTRAINTS_OR_SCENARIOS", "RESOLVES_EVALUATED_CANDIDATE_ELEMENTS_TO_SINGLE_RESULT", "INTERPRETS_REQUIREMENTS_FOR_ACTION_ADMISSIBILITY", "INITIATES_DETACHED_ASYNCHRONOUS_EXECUTION", "REPORTS_ABSENT_OR_UNAVAILABLE_CAPABILITY", "IDENTIFIES_SPECIFIC_POTENTIAL_FAILURE_MODE", "ASSESSES_COMPETING_ACCOUNTS_OF_SAME_OBSERVATION", "ESTABLISHES_EVIDENCE_GROUNDED_TASK_OUTCOME_REFERENCE", "FORMULATES_STRUCTURED_OPERATIVE_ACCOUNT", "SPECIFIES_TARGET_LINKED_CONCRETE_MEANS", "GROUNDS_COMPUTATIONAL_ASSESSMENT_IN_QUANTITATIVE_ANALYSIS"]

Read every member's complete definition, ordered parameters, assertion conditions, and exclusion conditions. Identify the common underlying behavioral mechanism and generate exactly one complete predicate following the system instructions. The new predicate must preserve the cluster arity. Use a unique predicate name that does not conflict with previously generated predicate names. Return only the complete five-field JSON predicate.

message.content:
{
  "name": "ANTICIPATES_PROSPECTIVE_VERIFICATION",
  "definition": "The reasoning identifies or assesses one or more prospective verification, testing, or evaluation activities aimed at confirming an action outcome, validating robustness beyond baseline coverage, or determining whether a solution would satisfy anticipated acceptance conditions. The prospective checks may include planned post-action checks, additional input variations not exercised by given tests, or unstated evaluator scenarios, provided that at least one identifiable verification target, criterion, input variation, usage pattern, or external check is present and the reasoning connects it to a validation or assurance purpose.",
  "parameters": [
    {
      "name": "reasoning",
      "type": "reasoning",
      "description": "Reasoning text that names or assesses prospective verification checks, test variations, usage scenarios, or evaluator conditions and relates them to confirming an outcome, reducing risk, or establishing solution adequacy."
    }
  ],
  "assertion_conditions": [
    "The reasoning refers to one or more verification, testing, or evaluation activities or scenarios that are prospective relative to already completed work, rather than solely reporting past checks.",
    "At least one identifiable verification target or criterion is present, such as an action outcome or final state, an untested input variation, an alternative usage pattern, or an unstated external evaluator check.",
    "The reasoning links the prospective check to a validation or assurance purpose, such as confirming that an action produced the required outcome, increasing confidence in robustness beyond existing coverage, or determining whether the solution would satisfy an anticipated acceptance condition."
  ],
  "exclusion_conditions": [
    "The reasoning only describes exploratory inspection before any relevant action or implementation and does not identify a prospective verification target or validation purpose.",
    "The reasoning only reports checks already completed or results already obtained without identifying any future, additional, or anticipated verification or evaluation target.",
    "The reasoning states only a generic next step or action without any verification, testing, evaluation, or assurance purpose.",
    "The reasoning describes hypothetical environment or user behavior without connecting it to verification, evaluation, or acceptance of the solution.",
    "The reasoning merely restates specified requirements or required tests without committing to any prospective check or assessing robustness against any anticipated verification condition."
  ]
}

